Now check whether your patch fired. On fremont:

bash
cd ~/work/ascend/AscendNPU-IR
sed -n '181960,182100p' ~/mr3160_full.log | grep -n "memref.alloc"

That's the IR right after the first ConstantizeBufferSize run. What you're looking for is memref.alloc with ? in its type versus fully static dimensions. Your patch's entire purpose is turning a dynamic dim into a static bound, so:

bash
awk 'NR>=181960 && NR<=182994' ~/mr3160_full.log | grep -c "memref.alloc.*?x"
awk 'NR>=181960 && NR<=182994' ~/mr3160_full.log | grep "memref.alloc" | head -10

If no allocs still carry ?, the pass constantized everything, and your patch may or may not have been the reason. To prove it was, compare against a build without your patch. You still have build-ubuntu-stale or can stash the change:

bash
git stash
# rebuild, re-dump, compare alloc shapes
git stash pop
